Test rg54: literals that read a symbol not yet defined
// Each literal names foo, or zero, before it is defined, so the parser files it in
// the pool before its value is known.  Literals that differ only in an operator on
// such a symbol once shared one pool word, and all but the first loaded a wrong
// value.  foo is 0301, at an odd address so that & 1, | 1 and ^ 1 tell; zero is 0,
// so that - and ~ tell.  The comment on each line is the word its literal must load.
100/
    lac [foo]           // 000301
    lac [foo*2]         // 000602
    lac [foo&1]         // 000001
    lac [foo>>1]        // 000140
    lac [foo/3]         // 000100
    lac [foo<<1]        // 000602
    lac [foo+1]         // 000302
    lac [foo|1]         // 000301
    lac [foo^1]         // 000300
    lac [foo%3]         // 000001
    lac [1+foo]         // 000302, and the same pool word as foo+1
    lac [-foo]          // 777476
    lac [-zero]         // 000000
    lac [~zero]         // 777777
    lac [[foo]]         // the address of foo's own literal
    lac [0]             // 000000
    lac [foo-1          // 000300
    hlt
    constants

301/
foo,    0
0/
zero,   0
stop
